{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034345-tass-mana-equivalents","id":1034345,"title":"Tass/Mana Equivalents","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-18T17:28:05-08:00","id":1034345,"title":"Tass/Mana Equivalents","content":"I've got a player who is playing an alchemist type mage who is interested in transmuting magical energies/materials (E.g mana/tass) which I confess to knowing very little about. I know that actually accomplishing that would require arch mastery but is there a way for them to study them more? For instance<br /> <br /> 1) I know Vitae is blood, but does it retain it's properties outside of a vampire? Could you construct a mystical vessel to contain it?<br /> 2) Would Goblin Fruit be a good facsimile of glamour as tass is to mana?<br /> 3) A spirit mage can turn essence into mana, but what about the reverse?<br /> 4) Does Pyros have any physical manifestation by itself? Would the heart of a promethean perhaps count?<br /> <br /> Only ever run mage so this this is what I've been able to piece together online. Sorry if I'm way off mark with any of these. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12891-polarbhang","name":"polarbhang","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T18:51:52-08:00","id":1034390,"title":"","content":"1. Vitae is contained in a Mandgoran Garden in some of the plants in the form of sap I think. <br /> 2. Goblin Fruit is less predictable then Tass and it's possible effects for more varied, but yes.<br /> 3. Maybe. <br /> 4. Firestorms and maybe vitroil. <br /> <br /> We also know the in 2e Giest Plasm is caused by Ghosts manifesting, and is the same substance as ectoplasm, so Mages can make the Bounds magical fuel easily and in large quanities.<br /> <br /> Mages can't directly effect Vitae, but they can effect the medium blood that contains it and the human body that produces it. So a Mage can cast a spell that allows a human a vampire is feeding from to regenerate his/her blood at an extremely rapid rate,effectively producing more vitae, a mage can cast a spell adding a magical effect to the blood that effects anyone who drinks it.<br /> <br /> A Mage can enhance a Changeling stats so that harvesting emotions nets more glamour, can cause someone to sleep and dream so their dreams can be harvested.<br /> <br /> Actually if the Mage has access to the Hedge, the Hedge is made up of Glamour I believe and anyone can learn to manipulate the Hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T19:20:24-08:00","id":1034407,"title":"","content":"Vitae is not blood, it's Life distilled from blood.<br /> <br /> Mages need Channel Essence to turn Mana into Essence, they can do it with a familiar bond as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T06:39:35-08:00","id":1034557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034345-tass-mana-equivalents?p=1034407#post1034407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vitae is not blood, it's Life distilled from blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>More accurate is that Vitae is <i>Life Force</i>, for vampire packaged in the blood. But for example Strix are also getting Vitea, but from stealing breath of others, not the blood of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T08:04:54-08:00","id":1034604,"title":"","content":"That's a good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T01:29:49-08:00","id":1036495,"title":"","content":"How about Sekhem from Mummy? They're most commonly found in Vessels, which don't neccessarily need Iremite descent. There's also that bit in Dark Eras where mages of Kemet (Egypt) knew about the presence of the Scorpion Empire, aka Irem, and the poisonous relics their god-kings and necromancer-priests left behind, so there's some historical precedent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T03:45:51-08:00","id":1036521,"title":"","content":"One of the devs once talked about Mages steering clear of sekhem because to a Mage it's like being asked to handle raw, radio active material without protection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T06:18:33-08:00","id":1036570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034345-tass-mana-equivalents?p=1036521#post1036521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the devs once talked about Mages steering clear of sekhem because to a Mage it's like being asked to handle raw, radio active material without protection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that was also on the history bit if I remember correctly. Which is exactly why I suggested it - just think of the shenanigans it would cause! (evil grin)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T18:06:55-08:00","id":1056395,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone, Y'all have been a real help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12891-polarbhang","name":"polarbhang","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","val